WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
Heat one spot on a metal bar.

2
00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:07.440
The warmth spreads out along it, and
never gathers itself back into one spot.

3
00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:11.060
Physicists track this with
a quantity called entropy.

4
00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.120
From solid, to liquid,
to gas, entropy rises.

5
00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:19.870
And a law of physics says that,
overall, entropy never decreases.

6
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.440
Yet water can freeze into
a neat, ordered crystal.

7
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.040
Its entropy falls.

8
00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:26.860
So how is that allowed?

9
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:29.680
In this mission, you'll
see what entropy measures,

10
00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:33.050
and why heat only ever
flows from hot to cold.

11
00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.120
Then you'll find out why
entropy, unlike energy,

12
00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:37.880
is not conserved.

13
00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:42.650
Your mission: explain how freezing water
can lose entropy without breaking the

14
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:43.230
law.
